# Architecture

Local-first macOS diagnostics app. Tauri 2 owns the machine. React renders findings. Do not upload project data or add telemetry.

- UI: `src/pages`, `src/components`. Shell is `src/components/layout/AppShell.tsx`.
- Domain types: `src/domain/types.ts`.
- Diagnostic rules: `src/diagnostics`. Pure functions over a `ProjectSnapshot`. One failed rule must not fail the scan.
- Rust snapshot and allowlist: `src-tauri/src/{snapshot,security,probe,chrome}.rs`. Commands in `src-tauri/src/lib.rs`.
- Frontend calls only those commands via `src/services/tauri.ts`. Never pass a shell string from the UI.
- History is JSON in the app data dir. `.env` values are dropped in Rust before the snapshot exists.
- Executable fixes are only `npm install --ignore-scripts` and `pnpm install --ignore-scripts`, after an explicit confirm dialog. Copy and open-docs actions do not run commands.
- Sample project: `fixtures/sample-node-app`. It is labeled sample data. Do not invent scan results when a real scan is available.

Verify with `npm test`, `npm run typecheck`, and `cargo test --manifest-path src-tauri/Cargo.toml`.
